# Textual's /conn [server]: connected, it quits and dials again; offline it
# dials. A server named for it is dialled once, on port 6667 without TLS,
# then the configured addresses come back. A bad address is refused.
! welcome
! type console /conn
> QUIT :Textual GTK
? quitting
< ERROR :Closing Link
> hangup #1
> dial #2 irc.test:6667 plain
? notice Disconnected: quit
? notice Connecting to irc.test:6667
? connecting
! type console /conn bad!host
? line console One or more arguments are not properly formatted for this command.
? notice One or more arguments are not properly formatted for this command.
? connecting
! disconnect
> hangup #2
? notice Disconnected: quit
! type console /conn Other.Test
> dial #3 other.test:6667 plain
? notice Connecting to other.test:6667
! disconnect
> hangup #3
? notice Disconnected: quit
! type console conn
> dial #4 irc.test:6667 plain
? notice Connecting to irc.test:6667
? connecting
